---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout
  title="If we visited your website — Crawl Policy Index"
  description="Who Crawl Policy Index is, what we fetch, and how to ask us to stop."
>
  <div class="page-head">
    <p class="kicker">For site owners</p>
    <h1>We read your public rules. We do not read your pages.</h1>
  </div>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      If you run a website and saw us in your logs, this page is how to recognise us
      and how to ask us to stop.
    </p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      Crawl Policy Index keeps a record of what websites say about AI crawlers.
      We are not a search engine. We do not train models. We do not follow links into
      your articles or products.
    </p>

    <h2>What we request</h2>
    <p>At most three addresses per site, once per day:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>your crawl-rules file (<code>/robots.txt</code>) — the main one</li>
      <li>an optional AI-instructions file (<code>/llms.txt</code>) — often missing; a “not found” is still useful</li>
      <li>your top-level sitemap (<code>/sitemap.xml</code>) — we do not then fetch every page listed there</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We keep a copy of those files so we can check our work later. We publish counts and
      short facts, not a copy of your whole site.
    </p>

    <h2>How to recognise us</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>At most one successful request per file per site per day</li>
      <li>One request at a time to your server</li>
      <li>Name in the request: <code>CrawlPolicyIndex/1.0 (+https://crawlpolicyindex.org/bot)</code></li>
      <li>Server address: <code>178.128.255.20</code></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How to be left out</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href="mailto:exclude@crawlpolicyindex.org">exclude@crawlpolicyindex.org</a>
      with the website you want excluded (for example, example.com).
      We stop within 24 hours and keep a record that you asked.
      We will not keep fetching you. Future lists of sites will leave you out.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not want personal data. If a fetched file happens to contain any, we delete it
      rather than study it.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
